From: XProtocol Bot
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Take the window data lock once in SetIMECompositionRect.

The wineland child-rendering series made WAYLAND_SetIMECompositionRect take
the window data before text_input->mutex (the order text_input_enter uses)
and release it at the end, but kept the original wayland_win_data_get() after
the focus check. Since wine-wayland made win_data_mutex recursive, that second
get does not deadlock: it takes the mutex a second time, and the success path
releases it only once. The calling thread returns holding the lock, and every
other thread that needs window data waits on it forever.

Where Winds Meet sets the IME cursor rectangle when a text input opens (and
during loads); the game then froze: the main thread kept the lock, and the
vkd3d-proton submit thread and the Wayland event thread blocked on it. The
lock trace (patch 0011) recorded get, get, release from this function with
the lock left held.

Use the data taken at the top; the no-surface branch leaves its release to
the error path.
---
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_text_input.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_text_input.c
@@ -272,14 +272,10 @@
     if (!text_input->zwp_text_input_v3 || !text_input->enabled || hwnd != text_input->focused_hwnd)
         goto err;
 
-    if (!(data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd)))
-        goto err;
-
+    /* data is held from above; a second wayland_win_data_get() would take the
+     * recursive win_data_mutex again and leave it held on return. */
     if (!(surface = data->wayland_surface) || !data->ime_ref)
-    {
-        wayland_win_data_release(data);
         goto err;
-    }
 
     OffsetRect(&rect, -surface->window.rect.left, -surface->window.rect.top);
     surface_rect = map_rect_to_surface(surface, rect);
